          "text": "The value of a dollar; the unit commonly employed in the United States in reckoning money values. Chop dollar. See under 9th Chop. (Stromateus triacanthus), having a flat, roundish form and a bright silvery luster; -- called also butterfish, and Lafayette. See Butterfish. mint, intended for export, and not legal tender at home. It contained 378 grains of silver and 42 grains of alloy.",
